{"type":"text","timestamp":1794342268627,"sessionID":"ses_e38efc4fdffeqXVhq3G1tPpRUd","part":{"id":"prt_1c7222eb3001m8xF5PHd58wCCF","messageID":"msg_1c7212b06001BiDZZNiYoIHrQ6","sessionID":"ses_e38efc4fdffeqXVhq3G1tPpRUd","type":"text","text":"## Objective\n- Build a full-stack account service: Flask JSON API under `/api` with sign-in lockout (5 consecutive failures → 15-min lock, admin early unlock) and per-client rate limit (20 sign-in attempts/minute), plus a React/Vite/TypeScript + Tailwind frontend served by the same backend on port 8000, data in SQLite under `./data`, built from the workspace `Dockerfile`.\n\n## Important Details\n- Python 3.13, Flask 3.1.3, gunicorn 26.2.0 (deps unchanged, no new pip deps — stdlib only: hashlib/pbkdf2, secrets, sqlite3).\n- Frontend: React 19.3.1, Vite 8.3.5, Tailwind CSS 4.3.5 via `@tailwindcss/vite`; `npm run build` → `frontend/dist`; typecheck script `tsc --noEmit` added.\n- Login check order: validate body (400) → per-client rate limit (429, key = first `X-Forwarded-For` value else `remote_addr`, sliding 60s window, only processed attempts appended) → username lock (429) → credentials (401).\n- 429 responses always carry `Retry-After` (ceil seconds); lock retry ≈ 900, rate retry ≤ 60.\n- Login attempts (`login_attempts` table, per account, `ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 20`) record ONLY credential-verified outcomes; 429-rejected requests are NOT recorded (decided choice).\n- Lock state in separate `locks` table keyed by username (works for unknown usernames too); `failed_count` resets when lock expires or on success/admin unlock.\n- Admin: username `admin` reserved (register → 409); password from `ADMIN_PASSWORD` env at startup — set → admin row upserted; unset/empty → admin row+tokens deleted, login → 401 `code:\"admin_disabled\"`.\n- Token auth: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`, tokens stored in DB (survive restart). Admin endpoints: 401 without token, 403 non-admin.\n- Response shapes fixed: `/api/me` = exactly `{id, username, last_login_at}` (no is_admin; frontend shows Admin nav when `username === \"admin\"`); `{\"items\":[{at,success}]}`; `{\"items\":[{username,locked_until}]}`; timestamps ISO-8601 with `Z` (microseconds).\n- `data/` path = `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / \"data\"` (deterministic, = `/app/data` in container).\n- CORS headers added via `after_request` (`Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *`).\n- Sandbox has NO docker, NO browser/playwright; pip and npm work via registry cache; `/tmp/opencode` tool calls are denied — temp files must live in `/workspace` and be cleaned up.\n- Known environment rule quirks: commands referencing paths outside `/workspace` (e.g. `/etc`, `~`, `/tmp`) get denied.\n\n## Work State\n### Completed\n- `backend/app.py` fully implemented (register/login/me/login-attempts/admin locks/unlock/health/static SPA fallback, SQLite schema, PBKDF2 hashing, rate limiter, lockout).\n- In-process + gunicorn e2e suite (`/workspace/e2e_test.py`) fully passing: health, 201/409 register, 401s, lockout 429 with Retry-After 900, admin flows, unlock, attempts list (8 items then capped at 20, newest first), 21st login → 429 with Retry-After 59 `code:\"rate_limited\"`, other client unaffected, session/account persistence across restart, admin-disabled phase.\n- Frontend written: `src/api.ts`, `src/format.ts`, `src/App.tsx`, `src/SignInForms.tsx` (429 message + live countdown \"Try again in Xs\"), `src/AccountPage.tsx`, `src/AdminPage.tsx`, `src/index.css` (`@import \"tailwindcss\";`), `main.tsx`, `tsconfig.json`, `vite.config.ts` (tailwindcss plugin), `index.html` title \"Accounts\", `package.json` (new devDeps: `@tailwindcss/vite` 4.3.5, `tailwindcss` 4.3.5, `typescript` ^5.9, `@types/react`/`@types/react-dom` ^19.2).\n- `npm install` + `npm run typecheck` + `npm run build` all pass; `npm ci` verified working (needed by Dockerfile); CSS contains Tailwind classes.\n- `pip install --user flask==3.1.3 gunicorn==26.2.0` done for local testing.\n\n### Active\n- Diagnosing that the Dockerfile's pip step (`pip install --no-cache-dir -r backend/requirements.txt -c backend/requirements.lock`) FAILS with pip 25.1.1: hashes in `requirements.lock` (constraints) auto-enable `--require-hashes`, then requirements.txt entries lack `--hash`/`==` pins → error:\n  `ERROR: Hashes are required in --require-hashes mode, but they are missing from some requirements... flask==3.1.3 --hash=sha256:f4bcbefc124291925f1a26446da31a5178f9483862233b23c0c96a20701f670c`\n- Confirmed identical failure in clean venv `/workspace/.venv-pip` (pip 25.1.1) with the exact Dockerfile command — so the base `Dockerfile` pip step is broken as-is (python:3.13-slim likely ships similar pip).\n\n### Blocked\n- No Docker available locally to verify image build; pip constraints+hash combination fails as described above (needs fix before image build can succeed).\n\n## Next Move\n1. Fix pip install so the Dockerfile command works under both require-hashes and normal modes: rewrite `backend/requirements.txt` to contain the full pinned list with `--hash=sha256:` lines (duplicate `backend/requirements.lock` content, minus `# via`/`-r` comments), keeping `requirements.lock` as the constraints file per README; verify with `python3 -m venv` + the exact Dockerfile command (and ideally a second pip version).\n2. Re-run `/workspace/e2e_test.py` after the fix, then clean up temp artifacts: `/workspace/e2e_test.py`, `/workspace/data/`, `/workspace/backend/__pycache__/`, `/workspace/.venv-pip`, and consider adding a `.gitignore` (`node_modules/`, `frontend/dist/`, `data/`, `__pycache__/` — also stops Tailwind v4 auto-scanning `dist/`, which changed CSS size between builds: 14.31 kB vs 16.43 kB).\n\n## Relevant Files\n- `/workspace/backend/app.py`: full Flask API implementation (auth, lockout, rate limit, admin, static serving).\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.txt`: currently only `flask==3.1.3`, `gunicorn==26.2.0` — needs full pins+hashes to fix Docker pip step.\n- `/workspace/backend/requirements.lock`: resolved versions with hashes, used as pip constraints (triggers require-hashes).\n- `/workspace/Dockerfile`: frontend node stage (`npm ci`, `npm run build`) then python stage with the failing pip command; port 8000, copies `frontend/dist`.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/App.tsx`: main UI state/routing (views: auth forms, Account, Admin nav for `admin`).\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/SignInForms.tsx`: sign-in/register forms with 429 lockout/rate-limit messages and countdown.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/AccountPage.tsx`, `/workspace/frontend/src/AdminPage.tsx`: account details/attempts table; admin locks table with Unlock buttons.\n- `/workspace/frontend/src/api.ts`: `request()` helper, `ApiResult`, `messageFrom()`.\n- `/workspace/e2e_test.py`: temporary end-to-end test script (delete before finishing).\n- `/workspace/README.md`, `/workspace/.dockerignore`: run contract and build ignores.","time":{"start":1794342268595,"end":1794342268598}}}
