{"type":"text","timestamp":1794342303165,"sessionID":"ses_e38efc4fdffeqXVhq3G1tPpRUd","part":{"id":"prt_1c722b5a5001DMGp2xbNpMwykC","messageID":"msg_1c7227afd001PIGPg8gKKrRTlM","sessionID":"ses_e38efc4fdffeqXVhq3G1tPpRUd","type":"text","text":"Everything is green. The project is complete:\n\n**Backend** (`backend/app.py`): Flask API under `/api` — register (201/409, admin reserved), login (200 token / 401), per-client rate limit (20/min sliding window → 429 + `Retry-After ≤60`), 5-consecutive-failure lockout (15 min → 429 + `Retry-After ≈900`, credential-verified attempts only), `GET /api/me`, login-attempts list (20 newest), admin lock list + unlock, SQLite in `./data`, PBKDF2 hashing, admin gated by `ADMIN_PASSWORD`.\n\n**Frontend** (React/TS/Vite/Tailwind 4): sign-in/register forms with 429 lockout/limit messages + live countdown, account page (last sign-in + attempts table), Admin nav/page with locked usernames + Unlock buttons, served by the backend on port 8000.\n\n**Dockerfile fixes**: `requirements.lock` converted to pure version constraints (hashes were triggering pip's require-hashes mode, breaking `pip install -r requirements.txt -c requirements.lock`) — verified with pip 24.0 and 25.1.1; `npm ci` verified.\n\n**Verified**: full e2e suite passed (lockout, rate limit, unlock, persistence across restart, admin-disabled phase), typecheck + deterministic build pass, CORS/preflight confirmed on gunicorn, temp artifacts cleaned (only `.gitignore`s added).","time":{"start":1794342303141,"end":1794342303143}}}
